.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt HOSTNAME 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm hostname
.Nd write or set the name of the host
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl s | d
.Op Ar name-of-host
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
writes the name of the host, or, given
.Ar name-of-host ,
sets it, which only the superuser may do.
The name is normally set at boot from
.Va hostname
in
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Write only what follows the first dot, the domain (the whole name if it has
no dot).
.It Fl f
Write the fully qualified name, which the name already is: accepted and
ignored, as on
.Fx .
.It Fl s
Write only what precedes the first dot.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gethostname 3 ,
.Xr sethostname 3 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command appeared in
.Bx 4.2 .
